 - English: \"My throat hurts and I'm very tired.\"\nCue 83 = 00:05:46 - English: \"Since when?\"\nCue 84 = 00:05:49 - English: \"Since last night.\"\nCue 85 = 00:05:53 - English: \"Do you have a fever?\"\nCue 86 = 00:05:56 - English: \"I don't think so, but I'm not sure.\"\nCue 87 = 00:06:00 - English: \"I recommend these throat lozenges.\"\nCue 88 = 00:06:05 - English: \"Take one every four hours.\"\nCue 89 = 00:06:09 - English: \"Can I take them on an empty stomach?\"\nCue 90 = 00:06:13 - English: \"Better after eating.\"\nCue 91 = 00:06:17 - English: \"And drink plenty of water.\"\nCue 92 = 00:06:20 - English: \"And if I don't get better?\"\nCue 93 = 00:06:24 - English: \"If you don't improve in three days, go to the doctor.\"\nCue 94 = 00:06:28 - English: \"All right. How much do I owe you?\"\nCue 95 = 00:06:32 - English: \"Six euros twenty.\"\nCue 96 = 00:06:36 - English: \"Here you are.\"\nCue 97 = 00:06:39 - English: \"Get well soon.\"\nCue 98 = 00:06:42 - English: \"Thank you, that's very kind.\"\nCue 99 = 00:06:52 - English: \"Finally! I thought you weren't coming.\"\nCue 100 = 00:06:57 - English: \"Sorry, I'm late again.\"\nCue 101 = 00:07:00 - English: \"Don't worry. I've just arrived.\"\nCue 102 = 00:07:04 - English: \"Here's your umbrella. It saved my life.\"\nCue 103 = 00:07:09 - English: \"How did the viewing go?\"\nCue 104 = 00:07:12 - English: \"Very well. I love the flat.\"\nCue 105 = 00:07:16 - English: \"And the price?\"\nCue 106 = 00:07:20 - English: \"A bit expensive, but it's worth it.\"\nCue 107 = 00:07:24 - English: \"Are you going to take it?\"\nCue 108 = 00:07:27 - English: \"I think so. I'll write to the owner tomorrow.\"\nCue 109 = 00:07:32 - English: \"Congratulations! We have to celebrate.\"\nCue 110 = 00:07:36 - English: \"What will you have?\"\nCue 111 = 00:07:39 - English: \"What do you recommend?\"\nCue 112 = 00:07:43 - English: \"The paella is very good today.\"\nCue 113 = 00:07:46 - English: \"Then two paellas, please.\"\nCue 114 = 00:07:50 - English: \"And a bottle of still water.\"\nCue 115 = 00:07:55 - English: \"Right away.\"\nCue 116 = 00:07:57 - English: \"Hey, are you OK? You don't look well.\"\nCue 117 = 00:08:01 - English: \"I've got a bit of a cold, that's all.\"\nCue 118 = 00:08:06 - English: \"You should rest this weekend.\"\nCue 119 = 00:08:10 - English: \"You're right. But I have a thousand things to do.\"\nCue 120 = 00:08:15 - English: \"Shall I give you a hand with the move?\"\nCue 121 = 00:08:19 - English: \"Really? That would be great.\"\nCue 122 = 00:08:23 - English: \"Of course. That's what friends are for.\"\nCue 123 = 00:08:27 - English: \"I owe you one, again.\"\nCue 124 = 00:08:31 - English: \"You owe me two. But who's counting?\"\nCue 125 = 00:08:35 - English: \"What do you mean by that?\"\nCue 126 = 00:08:39 - English: \"That you buy me the next dinner.\"\nCue 127 = 00:08:43 - English: \"It's a deal.\"\nCue 128 = 00:08:46 - English: \"Here you are. Enjoy your meal!\"\nCue 129 = 00:08:50 - English: \"That looks delicious!\"\nCue 130 = 00:08:53 - English: \"To the new flat.\"\nCue 131 = 00:08:57 - English: \"Cheers!\"\nCue 132 = 00:08:59 - English: \"By the way, is it still raining?\"\nCue 133 = 00:09:03 - English: \"It's pouring.\"\nCue 134 = 00:09:06 - English: \"Then you're lending me the umbrella again.\"\nCue 135 = 00:09:11 - English: \"No way. This time I'll walk you home.\"\nCue 136 = 00:09:16 - English: \"You're a sweetheart.\"\n\nNow, we have to select 10 beginner phrases.\n\nWe can apply criteria:\n\nBeginner-level guidelines: short (2-6 words), everyday usefulness, simple structures, polite forms.\n\nCandidates (with approximate word counts):\n\n- 1: \"¡Buenos días! ¿Qué te pongo?\" - 5 words (Buenos 1, días 2, Qué 3, te 4, pongo 5) okay.\n- 2: \"Un café con leche, por favor.\" - 6 words (?) \"Un\", \"café\", \"con\", \"leche\", \"por\", \"favor\" = 6 words. Good.\n- 3: \"¿Para tomar aquí o para llevar?\" - many words >6. Not beginner.\n- 4: \"Para llevar